hi there its senior editor Kevin van Ord  standing in for reviewer Josiah and  Auden to tell you about Sniper Elite 3  in Sniper Elite 3 there's a guilty  satisfaction that comes from the game's  glorious slow-motion kills what the game  does best is on full display early on  and that's the grotesque and brutal  x-ray vision assassinations the level  design in Sniper Elite 3 is more open  than previous games in the series often  encouraging shots being fired for more  than 300 metres away each of the 8  locations in the campaign presents you  with a sniping sandbox where creativity  leads to better shooting and stronger  positioning rushing headfirst into enemy  territory is always an option but you're  likely to crumpled into the dirt after  just a couple of well-placed shots from  your enemies whenever you aren't sniping  sniper elite 3 can prove frustrating not  because the surrounding mechanics are  broken or the levels are poorly  constructed it's because every action  building up to you actually pulling the  trigger feels more like a chore than an  interesting setup for the perfect shot  I'll have to shoot from this side of the  canyon you're often faced with tedious  stealth sections littered with soldiers  who perk up as soon as you fire off a  noisy round clearing the map with a  silenced pistol or a knife as often the  best route to success that's not to say  that Sniper Elite 3 is overly  challenging however if you take the time  to spot and tag enemies before firing  you ensure that you have time to  relocate to another vantage point  immediately after taking your shot the  game rewards you for relocating  successfully though it's too easy to  simply backpedal to an area that you've  already cleared and then wait for  enemies to cool off too many situations  throughout the campaign encourage  close-range monotony over the wildly  entertaining sniping  you're not required to kill everything  with a heartbeat in order to progress  but the satisfaction that comes with  long-range marksmanship is almost too  great to pass up after locating a viable  target you have the option of steadying  your breath and adding a reticle that  shows you exactly where your bullet will  drop once you fire off that perfect shot  the camera follows it around as it  leisurely approaches its mark in that  very moment all that matters is the  journey of a single bullet  finale of the shot is primal bliss eyes  pop lungs burst and testicles rupture as  you pump round after round into the  opposition it's the feature attraction  of the series and it's better than ever  you kill hundreds of unsuspecting  enemies in this manner watching as  formerly distinctive faces are violently  torn beyond recognition  a handful of difficulty settings extends  the life of an otherwise stunted  campaign which features one of the most  forgettable world war two stories in  recent memory the deadly serious  dialogue hardly matches the over-the-top  kills so you can safely ignore the story  that's an officer yet on violence stuff  he has the key I'll be back for better  commentary bring a friend in to campaign  missions with some backup it can be  cumbersome to coordinate shots without  alerting the guards but adding a second  sniper to the mix creates a whole new  set of tactics to consider there's also  an asymmetrical co-op mode called  overwatch which revolves around spotting  and downing as many enemies as possible  but this is much less interesting than  the tactical challenges of working  through the campaign together  competitive multiplayer is light on  surprise and heavy on disheartening  deaths of course to discover this aspect  of online play you have to get into a  game most of the time however you just  end up disconnecting after spawning  failing to connect or crashing to the  PlayStation Force dashboard Sniper Elite  3 s multiplayer is mostly broken it's  almost too easy to forget all of sniper  threes head-scratching issues when that  bullet makes contact with someone's  cranium though it's a shallow crude  pleasure but the delightful disorder  that's just around every corner is  strong enough to overshadow an otherwise  forgettable experience  you
 

